---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import MediaCredit from "../components/MediaCredit.astro";
import site from "../data/site.json";
import { asset } from "../data/paths";
---
<Layout title={`Accessibility & media credits — ${site.wordmark}`}>
  <div class="reading-container">
    <header class="page-title"><h1>Accessibility & media credits</h1><p class="lead">The design target is WCAG 2.1 Level A and AA.</p><p>Automated checks support this research site's accessibility work; they do not establish complete ADA or WCAG conformance.</p></header>
    <div class="prose">
      <section><h2>Using this site</h2><ul>
        <li>The first keyboard link skips to the main content. Focus is visible and the layout reflows on narrow screens.</li>
        <li>Silent videos play when visible. Each native player provides keyboard-operable play and pause controls. A manual pause is remembered when you scroll away and return.</li>
        <li>Reduced-motion and data-saving preferences prevent automatic playback. Native controls still let you choose to play. Moving a video out of view or hiding the tab pauses it.</li>
        <li>All videos show complete frames and have no audio track. Complete text alternatives and timed visual descriptions accompany them. On narrow screens, paired videos stack vertically.</li>
        <li>Method and setting figures have descriptive alternatives and expandable explanations. Their meaning is described in words as well as labels; color alone is not required.</li>
        <li>Core research content and native media controls remain available without JavaScript. The citation can be selected as text.</li>
      </ul></section>
      <section><h2>Media scope and sources</h2><p>The Waymo video provides independent real-world context; it is not a road test of the paper's controller. The title and body SUMO clips are different excerpts from the same author-supplied <cite>TL_medium.mp4</cite> recording. They illustrate the simulation setting, without establishing the controller, robot-vehicle share, or performance of a particular configuration.</p><p>All excerpts have complete linked text alternatives and consolidated descriptions in the media notes. Original recording speed and complete frames are retained, and the digitally silent source audio is omitted. The original video remains unchanged.</p></section>
      <section id="attachments"><h2>Paper and research materials</h2><p>The <a href={site.paperUrl}>published paper</a> provides the complete study. A <a href={site.htmlPaper}>full preprint in HTML</a> is also available; it is a preprint version, not a guaranteed identical copy of the published article.</p><p>The supplied publisher PDF is untagged and remains unchanged. External PDFs have not been fully assessed for tags, reading order, mathematical accessibility, or assistive-technology behavior. Original research data are preserved in the repository; the website presents a concise qualitative overview.</p><p>Method and intersection illustrations come from the authors' ground-traffic proposal slides. The network figure comes from the published paper. Sources and complete explanations accompany the <a href={`${asset()}#method`}>method figures</a> and <a href={`${asset()}#results`}>network setting figure</a>. Rights in third-party media remain with their respective holders.</p></section>
      <section><h2>Checks and remaining review</h2><p>The deployment workflow includes axe-core checks against WCAG 2.1 A/AA rules, keyboard navigation, native media controls, reduced-motion and data-saving behavior, image alternatives, narrow-screen reflow, text spacing, and content without JavaScript. See the <a href={`${site.siteRepo}/actions`}>deployment checks</a>.</p><p>Screen-reader usability, scientific image contrast, external attachments, and review with users with disabilities require further assessment. This site does not claim an ADA or WCAG certification.</p></section>
      <section><h2>Report an access barrier</h2><p>Email <a href="mailto:liusongyang@ufl.edu">Songyang Liu at liusongyang@ufl.edu</a> with the page, content needed, browser, and assistive technology involved.</p></section>
      <section><h2>Privacy</h2><p>This static site serves its fonts, figures, and excerpts locally, without analytics or embedded third-party players. External links open the provider's site, where its privacy practices apply.</p></section>
    </div>
    <div class="section"><MediaCredit /></div>
  </div>
</Layout>
